From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dugs <dugahol@protonmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 17:05:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Input: apple_z2: Allow firmware without a SET_CONFIG record

The initial-config scan returned -EINVAL when no SET_CONFIG record was
present, forcing the device's real C1F5E,3 firmware to be replaced with a
synthetic C1F5E,4 container just to carry a config record.  Boards with
fixed_timing take their timing from match data, so no config is required;
accept firmware that has none.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/input/touchscreen/apple_z2.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/input/touchscreen/apple_z2.c b/drivers/input/touchscreen/apple_z2.c
--- a/drivers/input/touchscreen/apple_z2.c
+++ b/drivers/input/touchscreen/apple_z2.c
@@ -4520,7 +4520,8 @@
 		fw_idx = round_up(fw_idx + size, 4);
 	}
 
-	return -EINVAL;
+	/* No SET_CONFIG: boards with fixed_timing take all timing from match data. */
+	return 0;
 }
 
 static int apple_z2_boot_preamble(struct apple_z2 *z2, bool full_duplex)
